<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/column/main/dim_product_credit_rtng/brick_rating> a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    dcterms:description "TYPE DEFECT: declared hllsketch. Should be varchar(256) - it sits in a run of eight sibling rating columns that are ALL varchar, and Brickwork Ratings is an Indian credit-rating agency whose grades are plainly text. Near-certain cause: the column arrived 100% NULL and the loader could not infer a type. UNQUERYABLE - Redshift restricts hllsketch to HLL functions, so casting or comparing it to a string will ERROR. Treat as unavailable; any 'how many agencies rated this bond' count is wrong by one wherever Brickwork was the rater. EXPORT MISMATCH: the CSV has no brick_rating column; it carries brick_rating_count instead, blank on all 15 rows. The loader keeps this DDL name, so brick_rating loads 100% NULL. A count and a rating are different information - never map brick_rating_count onto this field. Both hllsketch columns in the DDL arrive with a _count suffix, consistent with the export having transformed the sketch type; whether the rating field was transformed or renamed, or a count is intended, is not stated by the source and must be confirmed with the data team." ;
    rdfs:domain <https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/table/main/dim_product_credit_rtng> ;
    meta:nullable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    meta:sourceColumn "brick_rating" ;
    meta:sourceSqlType "VARCHAR" .

