<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/column/main/dim_product_segment_map/segment_id> a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    dcterms:description "No dim_segment table exists - another ID/name pair with no backing dimension. 13 distinct IDs (601-613) for only 10 distinct names: three names carry two IDs each - 'Information Technology' 601 and 612, 'Energy' 602 and 610, 'Banking & Financial Services' 603 and 608. Every ID maps to one name. So COUNT(DISTINCT segment_id) = 13 while COUNT(DISTINCT segment_name) = 10; use whichever field the question or query names, exactly as supplied. Do not merge IDs or invent a replacement ID." ;
    rdfs:domain <https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/table/main/dim_product_segment_map> ;
    meta:nullable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    meta:sourceColumn "segment_id" ;
    meta:sourceSqlType "INTEGER" .

<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/column/main/dim_product_segment_map/segment_name> a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    dcterms:description "Supplied values (10 distinct): Automobiles & Ancillaries, Banking & Financial Services, Consumer & Retail, Defence & Aerospace, Diversified Conglomerates, Energy, Healthcare & Pharma, Information Technology, Infrastructure & Construction, Telecom & Media. NOT unique per segment: the 10 names are spread across 13 segment_ids, so grouping by segment groups on segment_id with segment_name; a plain list of names returns 10. The labels look like an industry grouping, but they are NOT the same values as dim_cmot_company_mstr.sector_name or dim_product_unified_cat.sector (e.g. segment 'Information Technology' vs sector 'IT - Software' / 'Electronics'), and the source gives no definition. Whether a segment is the same classification as sector or a separate grouping must be confirmed with the data team. Keep segment_name as supplied; never present segments as sectors or merge Segment and Sector into one category on label similarity." ;
    rdfs:domain <https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/table/main/dim_product_segment_map> ;
    meta:nullable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    meta:sourceColumn "segment_name" ;
    meta:sourceSqlType "VARCHAR" .

