<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/column/main/dim_product_unified_cat/benchmark> a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    dcterms:description "Intended link to dim_cmot_index_prices.index_name by FREE-TEXT MATCH - which, by exact match, finds nothing in this data (see below). NAMING TRAP: dim_mf_fund_complete calls the same concept 'benchmark_name'. There is NO index_id anywhere, so a spelling variation ('Nifty 50' vs 'NIFTY 50' vs 'Nifty 50 TRI') breaks the link SILENTLY, yielding no benchmark rather than an error. Populated on all 98 rows with 4 values: 'Nifty 50 TRI' (39), 'Nifty 500 TRI' (30), 'Nifty 10 yr Benchmark G-Sec Index' (28), 'Nasdaq 100 TRI' (1). NONE equals an index_name exactly (0 of 98): the TRI labels name total-return series while the price table holds price series ('Nifty 50'), the G-Sec label is spelled differently from 'Nifty 10yr G-sec', and Nasdaq 100 has no series at all. For the 30 funds it differs from dim_mf_fund_complete.benchmark_name on 19. Preserve each label and its unmatched status in stored data and the KG - never strip ' TRI' or store an alias. The ' TRI' strip in 01_domain_and_business_rules.md §3.8 is a QUERY-TIME house rule only, which an equivalent KG query must reproduce exactly as the SQL does. A verified mapping or matching series would be a separate enrichment." ;
    rdfs:domain <https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/table/main/dim_product_unified_cat> ;
    meta:nullable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    meta:sourceColumn "benchmark" ;
    meta:sourceSqlType "VARCHAR" .

<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/column/main/dim_product_unified_cat/bse_symbol> a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    dcterms:description "BSE scrip code. Typed INTEGER, which is substantively CORRECT (BSE codes are numeric, e.g. 500325) - but the shared '_symbol' suffix with the text nse_symbol invites treating them alike. NAMING TRAP: dim_cmot_company_mstr calls this 'bse_code'." ;
    rdfs:domain <https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/table/main/dim_product_unified_cat> ;
    meta:nullable "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    meta:sourceColumn "bse_symbol" ;
    meta:sourceSqlType "INTEGER" .

