""" .

<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/client_holdings/wsw_account_code> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: identifier
description: '-> dim_client_account_map.wsw_account_code. THE ONLY account-level join
  in the schema: no other fact table records an account, so account-level reporting
  is possible for holdings and nothing else. Sample 70001. ''wsw'' is a source-system
  prefix. Populated on all 505 rows (30 distinct codes). Of the 505 holdings, 174
  match an account-map row on code AND client_id, 210 match on code but the account-map
  row names a DIFFERENT client_id (e.g. holding 80175: client 7009, account 70017
  mapped to client 7010), and 121 carry a code absent from dim_client_account_map.
  A code match is a source-record match, NOT validated client ownership: never derive
  client identity through this join - use client_id directly for anything client-level.
  Reproduce a query''s own join condition exactly - joining on code alone gives 384
  matched rows; adding client_id changes the result. Keep both source client_ids and
  report the conflict; never invent a matching account. Whether the intended key is
  the code alone or code + client_id is not stated by the source and must be confirmed
  with the data team.'
display_name: Account Code
filterable: true
join_target: dim_client_account_map.wsw_account_code
name: wsw_account_code
nullable: true
sql_type: integer
type: integer
""" .

