<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_client_account_map/account_type> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: dimension
description: 'Uncontrolled varchar(256) with no declared enumeration. Observed values:
  Individual (30 rows), HUF (12), Joint (3), NRI (2) - a holder/ownership category,
  NOT a bank / demat / folio discriminator. It does not tell you which identifier
  group to read: Individual, HUF and Joint rows carry bank, DP ID and (on some rows)
  folio identifiers together, and the 2 NRI rows carry bank identifiers only. What
  account_type classifies is not stated by the source and must be confirmed with the
  data team. Keep the original label; never derive an account kind from it.'
display_name: Account Type
filterable: true
meaning_pending_confirmation: true
name: account_type
nullable: true
observed_values:
- Individual
- HUF
- Joint
- NRI
sql_type: varchar(256)
type: string
""" .

