<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_cmot_index_prices/index_name> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: identifier
description: "The safe key for this table, and the target of the two free-text benchmark\\
  \\ joins (dim_mf_fund_complete.benchmark_name and dim_product_unified_cat.benchmark).\\
  \\ There is NO index_id anywhere in the schema. Also unrecorded: whether these are\\
  \\ PRICE or TOTAL RETURN (TRI) indices - a fund's NAV return is net of expenses and\\
  \\ includes reinvested dividends, so a fair comparison needs a TRI. Check the actual\\
  \\ values for a TRI suffix before publishing any relative-performance figure. Five\\
  \\ values, 12 daily rows each (2026-05-04 to 2026-05-19): 'Nifty 50', 'Nifty 500',\\
  \\ 'Nifty Midcap 150', 'Nifty Smallcap 250', 'Nifty 10yr G-sec'. None carries a TRI\\
  \\ suffix - they are price series - and no benchmark label in dim_mf_fund_complete,\\
  \\ dim_product_unified_cat or client_holdings equals any of them exactly. Preserve\\
  \\ the names as supplied; the ' TRI' strip (01_domain_and_business_rules.md \\xA7\\
  3.8) is applied at query time only."
display_name: Index Name
filterable: true
name: index_name
nullable: true
observed_values:
- Nifty 50
- Nifty 500
- Nifty Midcap 150
- Nifty Smallcap 250
- Nifty 10yr G-sec
sql_type: varchar(256)
type: string
""" .

<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_cmot_index_prices/nav_close> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: fact
description: 'NOTE THE ORDINAL POSITION: nav_close is column 4, BEFORE nav_open at
  column 5 - the only place in the schema where OHLC is not in O-H-L-C order. Cosmetic,
  but SELECT * returns them in a surprising order and a POSITIONAL column mapping
  downstream would silently swap open and close. ALWAYS SELECT THESE BY NAME.'
display_name: Close
filterable: true
name: nav_close
nullable: true
sql_type: real
type: float
""" .

