<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_mf_fund_complete/obsolete_into_mstar_id> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: identifier
description: 'TYPE DEFECT: declared hllsketch. Intended as a self-reference to mstar_id
  pointing at the surviving fund a merged scheme went into - every other mstar_id
  in the schema is varchar(256). Near-certain cause: arrived 100% NULL, loader could
  not infer a type. THE FUND-MERGER CHAIN CANNOT BE TRAVERSED AT ALL. A fund that
  merged mid-period simply disappears from the time series, breaking long-run performance
  history and making it impossible to follow a client''s holding through a scheme
  merger. This is the one genuinely missing edge in the join graph. EXPORT MISMATCH:
  the CSV has no obsolete_into_mstar_id column; it carries obsolete_into_mstar_id_count
  instead, blank on all 30 rows, so the intended meaning cannot be read from the values.
  The loader keeps this DDL name, so the column loads 100% NULL. A count is not a
  replacement-fund identifier - never treat obsolete_into_mstar_id_count as one. Whether
  the identifier was transformed during export or the count is intentional is not
  stated by the source and must be confirmed with the data team.'
display_name: Obsolete Into Morningstar ID
