<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_product_credit_rtng/brick_rating> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: dimension
description: 'TYPE DEFECT: declared hllsketch. Should be varchar(256) - it sits in
  a run of eight sibling rating columns that are ALL varchar, and Brickwork Ratings
  is an Indian credit-rating agency whose grades are plainly text. Near-certain cause:
  the column arrived 100% NULL and the loader could not infer a type. UNQUERYABLE
  - Redshift restricts hllsketch to HLL functions, so casting or comparing it to a
  string will ERROR. Treat as unavailable; any ''how many agencies rated this bond''
  count is wrong by one wherever Brickwork was the rater. EXPORT MISMATCH: the CSV
  has no brick_rating column; it carries brick_rating_count instead, blank on all
  15 rows. The loader keeps this DDL name, so brick_rating loads 100% NULL. A count
  and a rating are different information - never map brick_rating_count onto this
  field. Both hllsketch columns in the DDL arrive with a _count suffix, consistent
  with the export having transformed the sketch type; whether the rating field was
  transformed or renamed, or a count is intended, is not stated by the source and
  must be confirmed with the data team.'
display_name: Brickwork Rating
export_mismatch: CSV header is brick_rating_count (all 15 values blank); intended
  field unconfirmed
filterable: false
name: brick_rating
nullable: true
sql_type: hllsketch
type: hllsketch
type_defect: should be varchar(256); landed on hllsketch (likely 100% NULL at load)
unqueryable: true
""" .

