<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_product_segment_map/segment_name> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: dimension
description: 'Supplied values (10 distinct): Automobiles & Ancillaries, Banking &
  Financial Services, Consumer & Retail, Defence & Aerospace, Diversified Conglomerates,
  Energy, Healthcare & Pharma, Information Technology, Infrastructure & Construction,
  Telecom & Media. NOT unique per segment: the 10 names are spread across 13 segment_ids,
  so grouping by segment groups on segment_id with segment_name; a plain list of names
  returns 10. The labels look like an industry grouping, but they are NOT the same
  values as dim_cmot_company_mstr.sector_name or dim_product_unified_cat.sector (e.g.
  segment ''Information Technology'' vs sector ''IT - Software'' / ''Electronics''),
  and the source gives no definition. Whether a segment is the same classification
  as sector or a separate grouping must be confirmed with the data team. Keep segment_name
  as supplied; never present segments as sectors or merge Segment and Sector into
  one category on label similarity.'
display_name: Segment Name
filterable: true
meaning_pending_confirmation: true
name: segment_name
nullable: true
