<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/dim_product_unified_cat/benchmark> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: dimension
description: "Intended link to dim_cmot_index_prices.index_name by FREE-TEXT MATCH\\
  \\ - which, by exact match, finds nothing in this data (see below). NAMING TRAP:\\
  \\ dim_mf_fund_complete calls the same concept 'benchmark_name'. There is NO index_id\\
  \\ anywhere, so a spelling variation ('Nifty 50' vs 'NIFTY 50' vs 'Nifty 50 TRI')\\
  \\ breaks the link SILENTLY, yielding no benchmark rather than an error. Populated\\
  \\ on all 98 rows with 4 values: 'Nifty 50 TRI' (39), 'Nifty 500 TRI' (30), 'Nifty\\
  \\ 10 yr Benchmark G-Sec Index' (28), 'Nasdaq 100 TRI' (1). NONE equals an index_name\\
  \\ exactly (0 of 98): the TRI labels name total-return series while the price table\\
  \\ holds price series ('Nifty 50'), the G-Sec label is spelled differently from 'Nifty\\
  \\ 10yr G-sec', and Nasdaq 100 has no series at all. For the 30 funds it differs\\
  \\ from dim_mf_fund_complete.benchmark_name on 19. Preserve each label and its unmatched\\
  \\ status in stored data and the KG - never strip ' TRI' or store an alias. The '\\
  \\ TRI' strip in 01_domain_and_business_rules.md \\xA73.8 is a QUERY-TIME house rule\\
  \\ only, which an equivalent KG query must reproduce exactly as the SQL does. A verified\\
  \\ mapping or matching series would be a separate enrichment."
display_name: Benchmark
filterable: true
join_target: dim_cmot_index_prices.index_name (free-text match)
name: benchmark
naming_trap: called benchmark_name in dim_mf_fund_complete
nullable: true
sql_type: varchar(256)
type: string
""" .

